story is highly suggestive of angina pectoris. On ECG, there is ST elevation in leads |, aVI, V5 and V6\n(lateral aspect of the heart) and ST elevation in V3 and V4 indicative of involvement of the anterior wall. The ECG\nis characteristic of an anterolateral ST-elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI).\nThe most appropriate management of patients with STEMI is emergency reperfusion therapy either by fibrinolytics\nor percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) if the presentation is within 12 hours after the onset of chest pain.\nSince the patient is in a tertiary hospital, PCI is the preferred method of reperfusion therapy.\nProvided that proper facilities and an experienced cardiac interventionist is available a PCI could be performed\nwith 90 minutes after presentation. Cardiac catheterization is a general term that includes angioplasty, PCI, and\nballoon angioplasty.\n(Option A) Fibrinolytics are the preferred method if PCI cannot be performed and the patient has no major risk of\nbleeding.\n(Options B and C) Aspirin and morphine have to be administered for every patient with acute coronary syndrome\nas important steps but they are the primary steps and can be given while the patient is arranged to be transferred\nto catheterization laboratory. Aspirin could be the correct answer if the question asked about the next step.\n(Option E) Rescue angioplasty is a term used to describe emergency angiographic coronary intervention after\nfibrinolytics fail to control the ischemia.","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["age","management"],"likely_visual_question":true,"parser_confidence":"medium","parser_mode":"v282_visual_page_asset","text_method":"source_page_image+best_available_text","parser_version":"2.8.2-residual-resolver-page-checkpoint-local-render-2026-09-23","stem_hash":"8bad1523f971e7ce537e6a949f18ea00f6864c47","duplicate_group_id":"exact-8bad1523f971","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"419672fe3ea5f42a2caf","record_type":"visual_mcq","source_file":"Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":91,"source_qid":null}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk,record_json=excluded.record_json,active_quiz=excluded.active_quiz,import_version=excluded.import_version,imported_at=excluded.imported_at;
