pancreatitis?','{"A":"A. Pseudocyst.","B":"B. Infection.","C":"C. Obstructive jaundice.","D":"OD. Pancreatic fistula.","E":"OE. Renal failure."}','E','Acute pancreatitis can be classified into acute interstitial (most common) and acute
hemorrhagic (least common). In the first type, the gland architecture is preserved but
is edematous. Inflammatory cells and interstitial edema are prominent within the
parenchyma. In hemorrhagic type, there is marked necrosis, hemorrhage, and fat
necrosis. There is marked pancreatic necrosis along with vascular inflammation and
thrombosis.

Hemorrhagic pancreatitis can rapidly result in severe hemorrhage, hypovolemia,
shock, and acute renal failure. Other options are also potential complications of acute
pancreatitis but often do not occur as early as acute renal failure.','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[3],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-4ef5b09a6509","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"3ba4bb482742f08b2fd3","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":3,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"3081f5d3aa4f0e8325cf","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GIT 1-40.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GIT 1-40.pdf","source_page":182,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"6273e61957cbff430d8e","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GIT 1-40.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GIT 1-40.pdf","source_page":183,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"9eb0374381e78ca9e4b5","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":513,"source_qid":"494"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"3ba4bb482742f08b2fd3","source_file":"Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":3,"supporting_pages":[3],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Gastroenterology","stem":"Which one of the following is the most common early complication of hemorrhagic\npancreatitis?","options":{"A":"A. Pseudocyst.","B":"B. Infection.","C":"C. Obstructive jaundice.","D":"OD. Pancreatic fistula.","E":"OE. Renal failure."},"source_answer":"E","source_explanation":"Acute pancreatitis can be classified into acute interstitial (most common) and acute\nhemorrhagic (least common). In t