d as a consequence of chronic\ngastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD). Hiatus hernia predisposes to GERD and indirectly to the development\nof Barrett’s esophagus.\n\nBarrett’s esophagus is a premalignant condition with a 40- to 125-fold increase in the incidence of\nadenocarcinoma of the lower esophagus; however, the absolute risk is relatively small and approximately 0.5%\nper year.\n\nEvery patient with alarming symptoms of weight loss, anemia, heme-positive stool, dysphagia, or GERD for more\nthan 5 years should undergo endoscopy and biopsy. Further management depends on the histological findings\nand is summarized in the following table:\n\nEndoscopy every 2-3 years for\nBarrett’s esophagus (metaplasia) lesions 2 3cm and every 3-5 years\n\nfor lesions <3 cm.\n\nLow-grade dysplasia Repeat endoscopy 6 months.\nHigh grade dysplasia Distal esophagetomy.","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["age","management"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"medium","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"0948a82343d8da0ffb0663ac77b3293f1ffb6e95","duplicate_group_id":"exact-0948a82343d8","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"d03a62daf5ac3cf42b77","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":9,"source_qid":null}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=