The walls of pseudocysts are formed by adjacent structures such as the stomach, transverse mesocolon,
gastrocolic omentum, and pancreas. The lining of pancreatic pseudocysts consists of fibrous and
granulation tissue; the lack of an epithelial lining distinguishes pseudocysts from true pancreatic cysts.

The mechanism by which a pseudocyst is formed is necrosis and liquefaction of the pancreatic necrosis
of pancreatic or peripancreatic tissue.

Pseudocysts can be seen in the following situations:

e After an episode of acute pancreatitis (in 10% of patients) - necrosis of peripancreatic tissue
progresses to liquefaction and pseudocyst formation. Alternatively, a pseudocyst may result from
parenchymal necrosis, leading to complete ductal disruption and gross leakage of pancreatic juice.

¢ In patients with chronic pancreatitis — pseudocysts may develop after acute pancreatitis attacks or
after the pancreatic duct is obstructed. The latter causes increased intraductal pressure and
leakage of pancreatic juice.

e After blunt or penetrating abdominal trauma (including iatrogenic injuries) - The injury can directly
disrupt the duct and cause leakage.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2025','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[15],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-08518d4fa778","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"a6dccef611929fac6892","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":15,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"5b1ff8f53c8a7b046e50","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GIT 76-100.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GIT 76-100.pdf","source_page":18,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
