roton pump inhibitor (PPI) therapy.\n\nNOTE - Of the symptoms, regurgitation is often more bothersome and more likely as a presenting symptom.\n\n(Options A) occasionally, achalasia may result from esophageal malignancy, especially at the gastroesophageal junction. However,\nesophageal cancer in a young patient with no known risk factors is far less likely than idiopathic achalasia. Moreover, with malignancy, a\nmore rapid course of dysphagia and a more profound weight loss compared to benign causes of dysphagia are expected.\n\n(Option B) In esophageal stricture, dysphagia for solids occurs first, and dysphagia for liquids develops later as the stricture progressively\nnarrows the esophageal lumen.\n\n(Option C) Scleroderma (systemic sclerosis) is a complex and heterogeneous disease with clinical forms ranging from limited skin\ninvolvement (limited cutaneous systemic sclerosis) to forms with diffuse skin sclerosis and severe and often progressive internal organ\ninvolvement (diffuse cutaneous systemic sclerosis). Skin involvement (including Raynaud’s phenomenon) is almost always present during\npresentation and diagnosis. Esophageal involvement in scleroderma may mimic the symptoms of achalasia; however, in the absence of\nother features of scleroderma, it is a remote possibility for this patient.\n\n(Option D) Esophagitis (inflammation of the esophagus) is associated with pain in swallowing (odynophagia) rather than dysphagia.","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","duration","therapy"],"likely_visual_question":true,"parser_confidence":"medium","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"deb47e250129819572cca553a6a620dadd44bc11","duplicate_group_id":"exact-deb47e250129","duplicate_sources":[{"record_